                "text": "**Analyzing Input Grid**\n\nOkay, I'm deep diving into the grid transformation problem. Train 1's input has me focused on understanding how specific rows behave. Row 2's structure of 8s, followed by row 3's combination of 8s and 7s, has me thinking about patterns. Row 4 and 5 seem similar but there are subtle differences to note. I want to clarify how these values are positioned and organized.\n\n\n**Discovering Symmetry in 7s**\n\nI've made a breakthrough. The 7s form a 3x4 block in Train 1's input. They're replaced by 8s, but also zeros. I realized this pattern maintains horizontal symmetry when transformed. I found the symmetry axis is at column 7.5. Columns 4..7 reflect to 8..11, and the relationship between 8s and 7s are key. The entire output shape is horizontally symmetric around col 7.5! The inputs of 8s are also symmetric!\n\n\n**Uncovering Rectangle Roles**\n\nI'm now focusing on the rectangle's function. Train 1 has a 3x4 rectangle of 7s, Train 2 a 5x4 rectangle of 2s, and the test input a 5x4 rectangle of 8s. In Train 1 the main shape is 8, Train 2 the main shape is 7, and test the main shape is 5. I think the shapes are transformed, not just masked. Train 2's output has only 7s, making me think 2s might be influencing 7s, or masked. I am tracing those influences!\n\n\n**Reflecting Transformations in Train 2**\n\nI've made a key observation regarding Train 2's transformation. The 2s completely vanish in the output, replaced by a reflected 7s pattern. Considering column 4 as the center, I noticed 7s in columns 1, 2, 6, and 7, which relate via reflection. Rows 3..5 contain 7s in columns 4..8, which transform to 0..8, perfectly symmetric. The original rectangle of 2s in the input seems to define which part of the output is being reflected, and which parts become zero. The 2's covered the left side of the shape, just like the 7s covered the right side! This mirroring could explain the 8s in Train 1.\n\n\n**Confirming Symmetry in Test**\n\nOkay, I've figured out the symmetry in the test input's transformation. The 8 rectangle, from rows 6..10 and cols 4..7, gives shape 5. Based on row 5 and row 12's columns, I've confirmed that the axis of symmetry is column 9. Reflections are matching perfectly.\n\n\n\n",
